      "extract": "A (strict) \\emph{Lie 2-group} is a Lie groupoid $\\Gamma$ whose objects and morphisms are Lie groups, and all of whose structure maps are Lie group homomorphisms. One can conveniently bundle the multiplications and the inversions into smooth functors \\begin{equation*} m: \\Gamma \\times \\Gamma \\to \\Gamma \\quad\\text{ and }\\quad i: \\Gamma \\to \\Gamma\\text{.} \\end{equation*} \\begin{example} For $A$ an abelian Lie group,",
