      "extract": "\\label{versionII} It is well known that for a Lie group $G$ the \\emph{smooth} \\v Cech-cohomology $ \\h^1(M,G)$ and the \\emph{continuous} \\v Cech-cohomology $ \\h_c^1(M,G)$ agree if $M$ is a smooth manifold (in particular paracompact). This can e.g. be shown by locally approximating continuous cocycles by smooth ones without changing the cohomology class -- see \\cite{wockel2} (even for $G$ infinite-dimensional). Below",
